================================================================================
ADDENDUM A - DEPLOYMENT PACKAGE GRANT
================================================================================

This Addendum applies ONLY to the contents of this repository
(github.com/lpanigrahi/nxpi_config) and prevails over the terms above to the
extent of any conflict. Anything it does not cover remains subject to those
terms without modification.

A.1 DEFINITIONS

   "Deployment Package" means the contents of this repository: the shell
   scripts, the Docker Compose and Caddy configuration, the pgBackRest
   configuration, the documentation, and the static SQL artifacts under db/.

   "Application Software" means the NXPi application itself, including the
   container images it is distributed as (ghcr.io/negentrophi/nxpi_dev and
   related images), its source code, and everything else covered by the terms
   above. The Application Software is NOT part of the Deployment Package, and
   nothing in this Addendum grants any right in it.

   "Authorized Operator" means a person or entity holding a current, valid
   written agreement with Negentrophi permitting it to operate an instance of
   the Application Software, or acting on such a party's behalf and at its
   direction.

A.2 GRANT

   Negentrophi grants each Authorized Operator a limited, non-exclusive,
   non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable, royalty-free license to:

   a) use, execute and run the Deployment Package;
   b) reproduce it internally as needed to deploy and operate the Application
      Software, including copying it onto the machines it provisions; and
   c) modify its configuration and its scripts for that party's own internal
      deployment and operational purposes.

   Paragraph (c) is deliberate and necessary: operating this package REQUIRES
   editing files within it - creating .env and .env.app from their examples,
   enabling the dedicated-disk volume options in docker-compose.yml, and
   completing pgbackrest.conf, among others. Section 2(c) above does not
   restrict those acts for an Authorized Operator.

   This grant extends to deploying, operating and maintaining the Application
   Software, and to no other purpose.

A.3 CONFIDENTIALITY DOES NOT APPLY

   Negentrophi publishes the Deployment Package openly. Section 4 above does
   NOT apply to it: the Deployment Package is not confidential, is not
   asserted as a trade secret, and no obligation of secrecy attaches to it.
   Section 4 continues to apply in full to the Application Software.

   The Deployment Package deliberately contains no credentials. The files that
   would - .env, .env.app, secrets/, certificate material, backups - are
   excluded from version control and are the operator's own confidential
   material, never Negentrophi's to publish.

A.4 RESERVATIONS

   Nothing in this Addendum permits any party to:

   a) redistribute, publish, sell, sublicense, rent, lease or otherwise
      transfer the Deployment Package, or any modified version of it, to a
      third party;
   b) remove, alter or obscure any copyright, license or proprietary notice in
      it, including this file;
   c) use it to develop, operate or support a product or service that competes
      with Negentrophi; or
   d) use, obtain, run or reverse engineer the Application Software. Access to
      the Application Software is governed solely by the terms above and by any
      separate written agreement.

A.5 UNCHANGED TERMS

   Sections 3 (Ownership), 5 (No Warranty), 6 (Limitation of Liability),
   7 (Enforcement), 8 (Termination) and 9 (Governing Law) apply to the
   Deployment Package in full. In particular, the Deployment Package is
   provided "AS IS"; it provisions, migrates and can destroy production data;
   and Negentrophi accepts no liability arising from its use.

A.6 REVOCATION

   Negentrophi may revoke or amend this grant at any time. Revocation is not
   retroactive as to deployments already made under it in good faith.

